            <div xml:id="d428">

                <pb facs="0598" n="502" sameAs="frus:frus1921v02/pg502"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.51/661: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Summerlin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-10-21T17:00:00-06:36"><hi rendition="#italic">October 21,
                                1921—5 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 10:35
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>196. Lamont reports failure of negotiations due to Government’s insistence on
                    attempting to carry out bond purchase clause of oil agreement. However, door is
                    left open for resumption of negotiations on sound basis when Mexican authorities
                    appreciate that bond purchase proposal is not workable.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Summerlin</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
